# React / Inertia Frontend Rules

## Pages

- One default-exported component per file in `resources/js/pages/`
- Path mirrors Inertia name: `dev-tools/console` → `pages/dev-tools/console.tsx`
- Always set `<Head title="..." />` from `@inertiajs/react`

## Cyber dev-tool page template

```tsx
import CyberShell from '@/components/cyber-shell';
import { Head } from '@inertiajs/react';

export default function ExampleTool() {
    return (
        <CyberShell>
            <Head title="Example Tool" />
            <section className="cyber-grid rounded-3xl border border-primary/15 bg-surface p-6 ...">
                {/* DEV_TOOL_XX // LABEL header, dual-pane input/output, cyber-tool-button actions */}
            </section>
        </CyberShell>
    );
}
```

## State & forms

- Local UI state: `useState`, derived values: `useMemo`
- Server mutations: `useForm` from `@inertiajs/react`
- Shared props: `usePage<SharedData>()`
- Routes: global `route()` from Ziggy

## Logic separation

Put pure functions in `resources/js/lib/<name>.ts`. Pages should be thin UI wrappers.

## Styling

- Cyber pages: Tailwind + cyber classes (`.cyber-tool-button`, `.cyber-input`, `.glow-text`)
- Admin/settings: shadcn `ui/*` + `cn()` from `@/lib/utils`
- Icons: `lucide-react`
- Dark mode: `use-appearance` hook — do not bypass

## Types

- Shared types in `resources/js/types/index.ts`
- Page-local types defined in the page file
- Export types from lib modules when reused

## Server fetch from dev-tools

Use CSRF token from `<meta name="csrf-token">` for POST requests to Laravel JSON endpoints (see `hash-generator.tsx`).
